        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For the DMS Parts Provision Team, the first step is to gather information about the part from the customer, including the make, model, and year."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening sentence implicitly starts the process (init) and describes the initial information gathering action (n2) with identical semantics."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once this information is obtained, the team proceeds to check the availability of the part in the local inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the inventory availability check step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "branch:b1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the part is found to be available locally"
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional clause opens the XOR decision node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "it is retrieved from the inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully represents the retrieval action on the positive branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the part is not available locally, the team records the customer's details."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the recording action triggered by the negative condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After retrieving the part from the local inventory, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly signals termination of the first process path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "then orders the part from Disuki."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the ordering step on the second path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the part is ordered from Disuki, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly signals termination of the second process path."
    }
